---
description: Golfolio project context and local Mac/iOS development workflow
alwaysApply: true
---
Read `CURSOR_HANDOFF.md` at the repository root before starting work. Read `outputs/the-golfer/MOBILE.md` for iOS commands and architecture. Check the current Git branch and working tree; preserve local changes.

The web app lives in `outputs/the-golfer`, not the repository root. The local Capacitor integration is on `codex/capacitor-ios`; main is older. Do not switch to main or overwrite the local integration to synchronize with cloud work.

Use real verified listing information only. Never add invented venues, players, scores, prices, photos, reviews, or fake live-status claims. Keep secrets server-side and exclude server files from the native bundle. Maintain existing authentication and admin authorization boundaries.

Make changes and validate locally. Explain the exact release contents before any merge/deployment and obtain user authorization for that release. Do not run Supabase SQL or change remote services as part of routine local setup.

For native changes, edit source files then run `npm run ios:sync` from the app directory. Do not hand-edit generated `mobile-dist` or `ios/App/App/public`. Use `npm run check:mobile` and `node scripts/check-venue-community.mjs` when relevant. Real device/simulator checks are still needed for native behavior.
